{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1823","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Unique Palindromes"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"palindrome"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is a string that reads the same backwards as forwards. For example, the string "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"abcba"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is palindrome, while the string "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"abca"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is not."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let $$$p(t)$$$ be the number of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"unique palindromic substrings"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of string $$$t$$$, i. e. the number of substrings $$$t[l \\dots r]$$$ that are palindromes themselves. Even if some substring occurs in $$$t$$$ several times, it's counted exactly once. (The whole string $$$t$$$ is also counted as a substring of $$$t$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, string $$$t$$$ $$$=$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"abcbbcabcb"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" has $$$p(t) = 6$$$ unique palindromic substrings: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bb"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bcb"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cbbc"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now, let's define $$$p(s, m) = p(t)$$$ where $$$t = s[1 \\dots m]$$$. In other words, $$$p(s, m)$$$ is the number of palindromic substrings in the prefix of $$$s$$$ of length $$$m$$$. For example, $$$p($$$"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"abcbbcabcb"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"$$$, 5)$$$ $$$=$$$ $$$p($$$"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"abcbb"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"$$$) = 5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given an integer $$$n$$$ and $$$k$$$ \"conditions\" ($$$k \\le 20$$$). Let's say that string $$$s$$$, consisting of $$$n$$$ lowercase Latin letters, is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"good"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if all $$$k$$$ conditions are satisfied "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"at the same time"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". A condition is a pair $$$(x_i, c_i)$$$ and have the following meaning: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$p(s, x_i) = c_i$$$, i. e. a prefix of $$$s$$$ of length $$$x_i$$$ contains exactly $$$c_i$$$ unique palindromic substrings. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"kind":"text","text":" Find a good string $$$s$$$ or report that such $$$s$$$ doesn't exist."},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Look in Notes if you need further clarifications."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains the number of test cases $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^4$$$). The description of the test cases follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$k$$$ ($$$3 \\le n \\le 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$; $$$1 \\le k \\le 20$$$) — length of good string $$$s$$$ and number of conditions."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of each test case contains $$$k$$$ integers $$$x_1, x_2, \\dots, x_k$$$ ($$$3 \\le x_1 \\lt x_2 \\lt \\dots \\lt x_k = n$$$) where $$$x_i$$$ is the length of the prefix in the $$$i$$$-th condition."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The third line of each test case contains $$$k$$$ integers $$$c_1, c_2, \\dots, c_k$$$ ($$$3 \\le c_1 \\le c_2 \\le \\dots \\le c_k \\le \\min{\\left(10^9, \\frac{(n + 1) n}{2} \\right)}$$$) where $$$c_i$$$ is the number of palindromic substrings in the $$$i$$$-th condition."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$2 \\cdot 10 ^ 5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, if there is no good string $$$s$$$ of length $$$n$$$ that satisfies all conditions, print "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Otherwise, print "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and a string $$$s$$$ of length $$$n$$$, consisting of lowercase Latin letters, that satisfies all conditions. If there are multiple answers, print any of them."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"le